2317: ## 29. The exact failed contraction in the unscaled H atlas
2318: 
2319: For the alternative with the original scalar fixed,
2320: \(N=0\), the H period matrix has rank one. In the
2321: good branch its primitive kernel is \(gh^{-1}\).
2322: The exact exceptional-base units of (SZ.62) give
2323: \[
2324:        Z\longmapsto wZ,\qquad
2325:        V\longmapsto-2\lambda w^{-1}V.
2326:  \]
2327: The transverse character is \(Y=ZV^2\), and the
2328: actual residual multiplier is
2329: \[
2330:                          Y\longmapsto
2331:                          4\lambda^2w^{-1}Y.              \tag{SZ.81}
2332:  \]
2333: In the reduced branch the primitive kernel is
2334: \(g^2h^{-1}\), and the transverse character is
2335: \(Y=ZV\). Direct substitution gives the same
2336: multiplier (SZ.81). These formulas retain
2337: the constants \(u_Q(0)=1/256,u_P(0)=16\) and
2338: \(u_X(0)=-1/4\); their ratios are exactly the
2339: displayed constants.
2340: 
2341: As \(w\) ranges over the exceptional base,
2342: the magnitude of (SZ.81) passes through one.
2343: Thus this literal rank-one H atlas has no
2344: uniform contracting quotient over that whole
2345: base. At a value with unit-modulus multiplier
2346: which is not a root of unity, its iterates
2347: accumulate on the transverse circle, so
2348: the action is not properly discontinuous
2349: there. This proves the failure of this
2350: particular unscaled quotient construction.
2351: It does not assign a return from the
2352: crossing, or obstruct a real orbit
2353: bordism retaining its exact multiplier.
